From: GPT-6.1-Sol <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: reject untrained links and track PHY init ownership

Resolve both medium display audit findings: exhausted training fails for
maximum and reduced links, and final bandwidth must meet the configured
capacity margin. Preserve the error through ordinary link cleanup.

PHY init/exit helpers now return errors and keep their own ownership bit.
Display callers publish initialisation only after success, unwind runtime
references on failed init, and do not perform AUX transfers after failure.
Internal exit/init pairs stop on errors; the next power-up retries a failed
reinitialisation without an unmatched phy_exit or incrementing init_count.
Local corrections to 0137/0145/0147; no equivalent upstream fix found.

Hardware: DP/native and HDMI hub replug, DPMS, reduced/max link policies;
inject all training failures, too-small downshifts and PHY init/exit failures.
Expect enable errors, balanced init counts, and successful later recovery.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
